From ab5ba43f31c64faf849375a40c9cc40fda01419d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iitimii <timiiowolabi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 19:51:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 34/35] S4.1: --draft-tier/--draft-k amortizer + vocab gate +
 ledger reservation

Path A per the D1 probe: the in-tree draft-simple speculator, wired into
gen_segment for unsegmented expert answers (router-hard and escalation
continuations). One spec round decodes [seed, draft...] as a single batch
on both mid and a new ctx_draft on easy's model -- under --stream-weights
the streamed ring walks once per round instead of once per token. Accepted
tokens stay decoded and are consumed through the segment's existing cut
checks; a mid-queue cut restores the pre-round checkpoint and batch-replays
the kept prefix (state always equals committed + emitted, the Q1 rule);
partial acceptance mirrors speculative-simple's restore-and-replay.

Guards: vocab gate at activation (n_tokens equal + probe tokenization
identical; --draft-tier front rejected naming 49,152 vs 248,320); the
draft is never silently demoted (ledger refusal names --draft-tier none);
explicit conflicting --tier-policy refuses; rollback capability derived
from hybrid append-only instead of the 2-token capability probe (RS8,
logged). Ledger: ctx_draft kv+compute itemized as new resident terms.

Measured (container, enforced 2048m cgroup, --ctx-expert 2048 --tier-ctx
easy=2048 --ctx-front 2048 -ub 32): ledger solves head-streamed (whole
4B streamed, W=1), math answer acc=1.000 at K=8, 3.2 tok/s streamed vs
~1.1 draftless, memory.peak 1975.8 MiB, exit 0. No-flag runs unchanged
(route s=1.056 reproduced).

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5
